{"authored" [{"question" "q-32139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+6y=46 \\\\ 8x+y=-23\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c72c700c448c2af12a1a7eec055362ede062cfde4e360a91101c1cb9ad6dc5e" "basis" 1087 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 1-6\\cdot 8}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{46}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}46 \\\\ -23\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/state.json" "file_sha256" "7c72c700c448c2af12a1a7eec055362ede062cfde4e360a91101c1cb9ad6dc5e" "basis" 1087 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003513/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32139" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacadem