n|  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "51e383b66a7c493103bd9ecd9597903735afe3c69fed707acfd713ea45ede6c8" "basis" 1180 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320803" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 7}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "51e383b66a7c493103bd9ecd9597903735afe3c69fed707acfd713ea45ede6c8" "basis" 1180 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-320803" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "53ad7294ab68a8da72a45b73d2d11026b24d6e022411f009ec40c3c1f268a